    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "5f846e3afde24f1f6f06addab75ecfe9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1339,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, our intention, as the present Government, is to put those structures into right use after completing them. This year's Budget has allocated or provided for the required financial resources to complete them and to make use of them for our requirements such as to build market places, trading places, support tourism sector activities, business activities and public activities and even for educational purposes, training colleges or for whatever purposes they are useful without taking further time.\n\nWe know it is an ambitious target considering the fact that this project has been going on for a long period of time. But, we are determined, with the help of the officials who are involved, to complete this and to ensure that we are able to give the benefit back to the people who paid and who are continuing to pay for the financial resources the then Governments had spent on those structures.\n\nSir, I will take this opportunity to mention the relevance of that initiative to this Debate going on at the moment. Those buildings, as I mentioned earlier also, were expected to provide services to the citizens and the businesses of this nation including the SME sector and our investors. Since I mentioned about the SME sector, I would like to give some update to the House on parate execution and the subsequent relief mechanism the"
