    "chunk_size_bytes": 1813,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cBy Gazette Notification bearing number 2430/2025 dated 28.03.2025, settlement notices totalling seven in number (Numbered from 5617 to 5623) for the Districts of Jaffna, Mullaitivu, Kilinochchi and Mannar covering more than 5,000 acres has been published.\n\nThe Tamil struggle for self-determination originated inter alia in response to the alienation of State land by the Sri Lankan State with the explicit intent of changing the demographics of the North-East, through which the Sri Lankan State attempts and continues to attempt to make the Tamils a minority in their own homeland. The Tamils have consistently maintained that their autonomous institutions must have control over State land in the North-East.\n\nThe above Gazette Notification is another initiative in the long history of depriving the Tamils of their homeland by successive Sri Lankan Governments.\n\nFurthermore, our understanding is that the land sought to be declared includes private lands which those private owners have difficulty establishing ownership owing to loss of documentation during the tsunami and repeated displacements.\n\nThis Government in its manifesto, both at the Presidential Elections of 2024 and the General Elections of 2025, promised to genuinely explore a constitutional settlement to the National Question which includes settling the question of who controls State land. However, this act on the part of the Government makes clear that their views are no different to the previous governments in relation to control of the State land. The Tamil people see this action on the part of the Government as yet another act of structural genocide of the Tamil nation.\n\nI urge that the Government immediately withdraw this Gazette Notification.\u201d\n\nSir, I am the Mover of this Motion, but you have given me only six minutes."
  },
