    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ef6fb4b01d4afe016337b67b207e3b46",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1360,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Minister, with the motives you have just stated, we would have no problems. But, the law you are trying to use has the completely opposite intention. So, if your intention is actually not to pronounce the lands you have demarcated, those 6,000 acres, as State land, this is not the law to use. What we are suggesting is what you have suggested doing with regard to land for wildlife and forestry. You appoint a committee or a commission, we will cooperate.\n\nAnd, I assure you, Hon. Minister, that you will have our cooperation in sorting out the problems of our people. I mean, why would we not want our people\u2019s problems be solved, whether it is your Government or any other government in power? But, I am telling you with utmost responsibility, you are using the wrong law to do that. On the contrary, this law, by the 28th of June, will declare all those 6,000-odd acres you have demarcated as State land. So, I kindly urge you to withdraw this Gazette. I assure you that all the Hon. Members seated on this side of the House belonging to the North-East, the Tamil Members, will cooperate with you. It is in our interest to solve the\n\nland issues which have been plaguing our people because they have lost documents. So, we understand the issue. But, this is not the way - you are frightening us and not even the Rajapaksas did this - to go about it."
  },
