    "chunk_text": "Sir, we have taken up another Gazette Notification for deliberation today. That is, Gazette Notification No. 2421/41 in relation to the Luxury Tax on vehicles. Under the previous taxation, the limit or the starting point for charging the Luxury Tax on petrol and diesel vehicles was Rs. 3.5 million. Due to the calamity that prevailed in the country and the depreciation of the rupee, the cost of vehicles escalated suddenly after five years when we started opening the market for vehicle imports. So, after five years, when vehicles are imported into the country, their value has risen up significantly, requiring adjustments to make sure that vehicles are affordable to the people. Previously, as the starting point, a Luxury Tax was charged on petrol and diesel vehicles when their value exceeded Rs. 3.5 million; for two other categories, the Luxury Tax was charged when the value exceeded Rs. 4 million and Rs. 6 million.\n\nOnce again, the reason why we are doing this is because, while facilitating this, we need revenue for the\n\nI will refer to the types of investments we are expecting as a country and the progress of those investments."
