    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dd2\u0db1 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0db1\u0da5 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dca \u0db4\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc7\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd. \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. M. Nizam Kariapper, PC) Hon. Presiding Member, when you spoke in Tamil, I think everybody was shocked.\n\nMadam, I wish to draw your attention to another important and critical matter that has gone unnoticed. Under the Ninth Schedule of the Constitution - Provincial Council List - matters relating to promotion of agriculture, fisheries, co-operative industries, cottage industries and local economic development fall within the jurisdiction of the Provincial Council. This clearly reflects the framers\u2019 intent that economic development of each province is not a central subject alone, but one that must be driven from the ground up with the Provincial Council paying a lead role. Ignoring this structure is not only a policy failure, but also a constitutional abdication.\n\nThe Northern and Eastern Provinces have distinct sectors with export potential, which could contribute meaningfully to the national economy. Let us start one by one. Culinary heritage and agro exports, traditional food items - you know about Jaffna traditional food items - organic products and preserved seafood from these regions are of high demand, especially among the overseas community. With proper training, packaging and marketing support, these items could be developed into powerful export brands. I will take an interesting example. When I visit Jaffna Courts, I go to \"Rasavin Wanam\". Just in front of it, there is a small boutique, which has a sweet item called \"elluppahu\" , a blackball full of nutritional value. You do not get that in any part of the country. So, these have to be promoted. I always go there and have that snack.\n\nThen, handloom and traditional textiles. Our handloom sector is a cultural treasure. It also presents a strong case for premium exports in the global sustainable"
