    "md5": "00eba6e474b580c4f1a1d6ec2496fa1f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2253,
    "chunk_text": "\u0b85\u0ba4\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb1\u0b95\u0bc1, \u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd \u0b85\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0ba9\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1 \u0b85\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bb5, \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd [\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb5\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bbe\u0bcd) \u0bbe\u0bbf\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bbf] \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae \u0bb5\u0b95\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd.\n\nWhereupon THE HON. SPEAKER left the Chair, and DEPUTY SPEAKER [THE HON. (DR.) RIZVIE SALIH] took the Chair.\n\nWhen we repeal the Foreign Loans Act, Sir, what happens is, we go ahead with the Public Debt Management Act we approved last year. Under the Foreign Loans Act, various agencies could borrow for the Government or sometimes, for State-owned enterprises and so on. But, now, everything is going to be brought under one place in the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development. Ideally this should have been an independent debt office, but it is still within the purview of the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development. So, hereinafter whether it is the issuing of a Treasury Bill, a Treasury Bond or the auction at the Central Bank, all these will be moved under the Treasury Office from the 01st of January. Also, there will be certain infrastructure and personnel issues that need to be resolved and I will let the Government explain all that.\n\nBut, I am going to take a critical view on what I see as a very oxymoronic situation here. Why I say that is, on the one hand, today, we are going to start making the Public Debt Management Act implementable because we are repealing the Foreign Loans Act. At the same time, the Hon. Kumara Jayakody presented the Sri Lanka Electricity (Amendment) Bill today. I am trying to show you how these are so contradictory and why it is not good for the progress of this country. Once you remove the responsibility of borrowing from the Central Bank and from other agencies and give the total responsibility to the Public Debt Office of the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, then, they will have the responsibility to borrow both domestically and internationally. When you take up borrowings internationally, we are talking about international\n\n1543 1544"
  },
