    "md5": "d2565f10f998b431ae398bc0e7f01022",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1167,
    "chunk_text": "But, I am going to take a critical view on what I see as a very oxymoronic situation here. Why I say that is, on the one hand, today, we are going to start making the Public Debt Management Act implementable because we are repealing the Foreign Loans Act. At the same time, the Hon. Kumara Jayakody presented the Sri Lanka Electricity (Amendment) Bill today. I am trying to show you how these are so contradictory and why it is not good for the progress of this country. Once you remove the responsibility of borrowing from the Central Bank and from other agencies and give the total responsibility to the Public Debt Office of the Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, then, they will have the responsibility to borrow both domestically and internationally. When you take up borrowings internationally, we are talking about international\n\n1543 1544\n\n2025 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 23\n\nsovereign bonds, with which this Government has promised to go to the market in 2027. Then, if we take other commercial facilities, that would be, for example, from the HSBC Bank or multilateral agencies like the World Bank, ADB and so on. Let us keep that aside for a moment."
