    "chunk_text": "So, what happened was, the Government guaranteed all kinds of facilities for all kinds of infrastructure projects of those SOEs without looking at whether they were able to pay back those loans. A lot of people say, \"We are out of bankruptcy\" and all that. But, how that is defined is when rating agencies remove a country from their default rating. Yes, Fitch Ratings and Moody\u2019s have done that, but the big one, the S & P - the Standard & Poor's - has still not taken Sri Lanka out of their default rating and the reason for that, Sir, is because the SriLankan Airlines is in default. It has borrowed US Dollars 175 million from the international market. Now, with the interest building up - the debt has not been serviced for the last couple of years - it has gone beyond US Dollars 200 million. So, what the S & P is saying is that they are not able to remove Sri Lanka from default status, meaning bankruptcy in the general language, unless the SriLankan Airlines is able to either restructure this facility or pay the loan. Currently, we are in discussion and I will come to that in a minute.\n\nComing back to the SriLankan Airlines, they are saying, \"Look, we will make these payments\". But, who will underwrite that risk?\n\nIf the SriLankan Airlines goes through this stress test, I do not know what kind of premium it would have to pay to the Government to borrow or to settle this loan. I honestly do not think that the creditors would agree to let just SriLankan Airlines undertake this responsibility without the Government coming in. So, ultimately, it is going to come back on to the State itself. Therefore, it would be a double jeopardy because we cannot pay the premium, in my view. If that is not the case, somebody could explain later on.\n\nThen, if the Government is not going to bring in private investments and is going to use taxpayers\u2019 money with SriLankan Airlines, what is the plan for the SriLanka\n\n1545 1546\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0"
  },
