    "chunk_text": "If the SriLankan Airlines goes through this stress test, I do not know what kind of premium it would have to pay to the Government to borrow or to settle this loan. I honestly do not think that the creditors would agree to let just SriLankan Airlines undertake this responsibility without the Government coming in. So, ultimately, it is going to come back on to the State itself. Therefore, it would be a double jeopardy because we cannot pay the premium, in my view. If that is not the case, somebody could explain later on.\n\nThen, if the Government is not going to bring in private investments and is going to use taxpayers\u2019 money with SriLankan Airlines, what is the plan for the SriLanka\n\n1545 1546\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nThen, coming back to repealing of the Foreign Loans Act, like I mentioned earlier, this US Dollars 50 million that the CEB is going to borrow is nothing. But, even to get that US Dollars 50 million, they would have to pay a massive premium to the Government, which the Ceylon Electricity Board cannot afford."
