    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1750228312097834.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-05-23-2025-05-23-0060",
    "chunk_index": 60,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "bfcf7296308e6a08af23d5c74a37bd0f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2070,
    "chunk_text": "Then, coming back to repealing of the Foreign Loans Act, like I mentioned earlier, this US Dollars 50 million that the CEB is going to borrow is nothing. But, even to get that US Dollars 50 million, they would have to pay a massive premium to the Government, which the Ceylon Electricity Board cannot afford.\n\nYou talked about building of a battery storage for the solar power generated. That is going to cost over US Dollars 1 billion. Let me tell you that the World Bank, the ADB and others are not going to look at commercially viable enterprises like the CEB in the way they used to look at in those days. They would say, \u201cLook, you go to the commercial markets. You have your own balance sheet; you have a credit rating. Based on that, you can get a government guarantee. If so, go ahead and borrow in the commercial market. We will look at fields like education and health, which are not commercially viable in the international markets\u201d.\n\nWhat I have to say, Sir, is that this move is good; this brings discipline. But, at the same time, you have to be pragmatic.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0db1\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva, you have exhausted your time.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0d82\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba\u0db4 \u0dc4\u0dba\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc2 \u0daf \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bb7 \u0ba4 \u0b9a\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbe) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harsha de Silva) I will wind up in 30 seconds, Sir.\n\nSo, you have to be pragmatic. I am actually being honest, totally honest here. You can operate within this new law you are bringing in today by repealing the Foreign Loans Act only if you open doors for private investments to come into infrastructure. Otherwise, you cannot. I will tell you today that at the end of this year, the Government would not be able to come anywhere near Rs. 1.4 trillion of capital expenditure promised. It cannot be done based on this new law you are bringing in."
  },
  {
