    "chunk_size_bytes": 1572,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d92 \u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db8, from tourism, we are looking at earning US Dollars 4 to 6 billion. Also, you must ensure that US trade tariff imposed by President Donald Trump is looked into. Worse than that comes the UK-US Free Trade Agreement they are going to sign. That will have a direct impact on us because we are a Commonwealth country and we have a very close relationship with the UK. We have De La Rue, which prints money, Marks & Spencer, Tesco, Primark and NEXT here. Ensure that more such companies are brought into the system. We had about US Dollars 1.5 billion worth of trade just about five years ago. Now, it has dropped to US Dollars 850 million. We must speak with other countries on our trade concern. The British High Commission in Sri Lanka should have asked us three, four years ago, \"India is going to sign a Free Trade Agreement with the UK and why are you all not doing it?\" We had a much closer relationship with the UK than any other country. So, ensure that we get back on the right track. And I hope you have the onus to get your team together and tell them to ensure that it happens.\n\nThen, the tax reduction. Madam Presiding Member, you know about this, as you have been speaking rightly in the Committee on Public Finance. Ensure there is tax reduction. I had been a Minister of Finance. So, I know the impact it has. We have 220,000 companies incorporated, but only 11,000 companies pay taxes. So,\n\nensure that we basically adopt a more rational approach towards that. Tax planning cannot be stopped and ensure that we bring an end to tax evasion."
  },
