    "md5": "9f3de534cfce78782f529f536fde9775",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1771,
    "chunk_text": "So, you acknowledge that the history has been so heinous to the Tamil people. You cannot say that a genocide took place without even being willing to make it a crime and then be willing to face prosecutions; that only makes it double-talk. I do not think the Government should go down that path. The Hon. Vijitha Herath must withdraw those comments because those comments are dangerous; those comments curtail free speech, make a mockery of human rights and give sinister people the authority, the stamp of a Minister, to go after people like myself, who genuinely believe that a genocide took place. I want to assert the fact that a genocide took place and want justice for it. Why are you running away from justice? We are asking for justice. We want a criminal prosecutory process that is independent enough and the only independent process that is possible is an international process. Why are you running away from that? Why are you not even being prepared to face it, unless you are guilty as charged? And if the Hon. Foreign Minister\u2019s intention is, in fact, to defend the guilty, then what he is doing becomes very clear. I do not think that it is the path this Government should take. So, he must withdraw those comments.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc0\u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) \u0dad\u0dc0\u0db8 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2 8\u0dba\u0dd2 \u0dc1\u0db1\u0dca \u0d89\u0dc0\u0dbb. \u0db8\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2 12\u0d9a\u0dca \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dda\u0dc0\u0dcf.\n\nSo, he must make it very clear.\n\nThe second matter that I wish to bring out is with regard to Kurunthur Malai, which is a very controversial site where the Sivan temple is located and by the way, a registered temple."
