    "chunk_text": "So, he must make it very clear.\n\nThe second matter that I wish to bring out is with regard to Kurunthur Malai, which is a very controversial site where the Sivan temple is located and by the way, a registered temple.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf, \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0dc1\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd6 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba \u0d85\u0dc0 \u0db1\u0dca.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc0\u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) I am finishing up, Sir.\n\nDespite that decision, Sir, the Buddhist monk in charge of Kurundi Viharaya has caught hold of the Police and the Department of Archaeology and has started arresting people who are doing farming in the area that former President Wickeremesinghe said should be given for farming; they are now arresting people there. Just two weeks ago, three people were arrested and one was a minor. The minor was released and the other two remain under remand custody even today. There is no Gazette Notification that is demarcating anything other than those 79 acres, which was gazetted in the 30s, with regard to Kurunthur Malai. But, despite that, the Department of Archaeology and the Buddhist monk along with the Police are going around arresting people. Is it not a rule of law problem? On what basis are you arresting them? So, the Government must intervene and stop that; that must be stopped. The Government\u2019s decision was taken over two years ago that those areas must be allowed to farm. Despite that decision and that decision not being reversed, for the police to be going around arresting people like this and for the Department of Archaeology to be working in an ad hoc way like this is just completely unacceptable. Therefore, I ask that the Government intervene and ensure that those people arrested are released forthwith.\n\nThank you.\n\n1607 1608\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbd\u0dda \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n(11th Start)\n\n2025 \u0db8\u0dd0\u0dba\u0dd2 23"
  },
