    "chunk_text": "The number of Tamil students studying NVQ Level 4 is, 63 and NVQ Level 5 and 6, 114 students. So, a total of 177 Tamil students are currently studying there. The number of Sinhalese students studying NVQ Level 4 is, 186 and NVQ Level 5 and 6, 40 students. Therefore, the total number of Sinhalese students is 226. The number of Muslim students studying NVQ Level 4 is, 21 and NVQ Level 5 and 6, 25students. So, the total number of Muslim students is 46.\n\n1717 1718\n\n\u0dad\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0dd2 \u0da5\u0dc1\u0db1\u0db4\u0dad \u0dc1\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dbb\u0db0\u0dba \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dc1\n\n2025 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 03\n\n\u2022 Automobile Technology\n\nAutomobile Technician\n\nAgricultural Machinery and Equipment Mechanic\n\n\u2022 Construction Technology - Site Supervisor\n\nDraft Person\n\nQuantity Surveying Assistant\n\n\u2022 Food Technology\n\nBaker\n\nLaboratory Assistant\n\n\u2022 Mechanical Technology\n\nMachinist\n\nWelder\n\n\u2022 Electrical and Electronic Technology\n\nElectrician\n\nSewing Machine Mechanic\n\n\u2022 Information and Communication Technology\n\nComputer Hardware and Network Technology\n\nICT Technician\n\n\u2022 Renewable Energy\n\n\u2022 Production Technology\n\n02. Initially, when this Institute was set up, the intention was to have it as a separate autonomous institute, but it was set up under the existing Act, No. 15 of 2017, under which the CGTTI was also established. At the time when the SLGTI in Kilinochchi was set up, there was advice from the Attorney-General\u2019s Department that the Act needs to be amended, if it is to be established as a separate autonomous institute. So, it required an amendment to the Act. But, that has not happened. It was in 2020 that the Institute was initiated and subsequently in 2022, the then Cabinet took a decision that it should be set up as a separate institute, but the necessary legal amendments were not made and the revisions had not happened. So, that is the current status and we are looking into whether that is feasible and whether amendment to the Act has to be made."
