    "chunk_text": "02. Initially, when this Institute was set up, the intention was to have it as a separate autonomous institute, but it was set up under the existing Act, No. 15 of 2017, under which the CGTTI was also established. At the time when the SLGTI in Kilinochchi was set up, there was advice from the Attorney-General\u2019s Department that the Act needs to be amended, if it is to be established as a separate autonomous institute. So, it required an amendment to the Act. But, that has not happened. It was in 2020 that the Institute was initiated and subsequently in 2022, the then Cabinet took a decision that it should be set up as a separate institute, but the necessary legal amendments were not made and the revisions had not happened. So, that is the current status and we are looking into whether that is feasible and whether amendment to the Act has to be made.\n\nstudents are facing. So, consequent to that site visit, we have allocated funds from the Budget, 2025 to upgrade hostel facilities and student welfare facilities. Those are really a difficult issues because the site is relatively isolated.\n\nSo, there are no services around for students to access either. Therefore, we are looking into that.\n\nWe are also planning to allocate funds from the Budget, 2026 to complete the construction of the hostel in 2026. Also, there is a long-standing problem about recruitment to this Institute in Kilinochchi. That also, we are addressing, and we have, currently, submitted the required cadre to the committee that looks into recruitment. We hope to get a favorable response from it soon and to recruit the cadre that is necessary to keep this institution going and to ensure that the services offered are appropriate."
