    "chunk_text": "[2.48 p.m.] \u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0db6\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dc4\u0dc2\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0baa\u0bc0\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0bb7\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Kabir Hashim) Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees, the Personal Data Protection (Amendment) Bill is of national importance. It was an Act that was passed with the intention of modernizing the legal framework for privacy and data governance, aligning Sri Lanka with global best practices, particularly with the European Union\u2019s General Data Protection Regulation. It was a forward-looking step. This was brought in 2022. But, for three years, this Act has been dormant and the core enforcement mechanism, which is the Data Protection Authority, is yet to be established.\n\nThe United Nations Special Rapporteur on Privacy, in a 2024 report said, I quote:\n\n\u201cData subjects find themselves in a position of defencelessness owing to their limited knowledge of the use that third parties make of information concerning them, since in practice they are unable to follow up on or monitor this use. This has repercussions for their ability to control their data - the essence of the fundamental right to personal data protection.\u201d\n\n\u0db8\u0dd6\u0db6\u0dbd\u0d9a \u0d85\u0dd2 \u0dad\u0dd2 \u0dc1\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0db4\u0dad \u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2 \u0db3 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0da7\u0daf\u0dd9 \u0d9a\u0dca \u0d87\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db1 \u0dc1 \u0d9a\u0dd2[\u0db1 \u0d91\u0d9a \u0d91\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc3 \u0d9a \u0da2\u0dc1\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0db0\u0dba\u0dc1\u0dda \u0daf\u0dd4\u0dc1 \u0dda\u0dc2 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc1[\u0ddd\u0da7\u0dbd\u0dad[\u0dc1 \u0d9a\u0dd2[\u0db1 \u0dc1. Now, the issue is whether your Amendment deals with that part."
  },
