d said that there had to be amendments. And, we believed that the NPP, which is supposed to be a people\u2019s Government, would be sensitive to the people\u2019s rights. But, I do not see that in the Amendment. That is the issue.\n\nThe shortcomings of the Personal Data Protection Act were described very well by a young researcher, Nida Admani, in the \"DailyFT\" yesterday. She says, I quote:"
