    "chunk_text": "\u0db4\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0dc1\u0db4\u0dad\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0db1\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca \u0db4\u0dad \u0d9a\u0db4\u0dad \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0. \u0d94 \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\u0da7 \u0daf\u0dd4 \u0dc0 9 \u0dc0\u0d9a \u0d9a\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dd0\u0dc1 \u0dc0\u0dc0.\n\n[\u0baa\u0bbf.\u0baa. 2.38]\n\nHon. Presiding Member, we are debating certain Regulations brought under the Anti-Corruption Act. I wish to state a few points with regard to my interpretation of what anti-corruption ought to be.\n\nSir, when a government acts in a way that its actions are so gross in nature and result in approving projects or various activities which are ultimately unsustainable to the point that it becomes impossible for the government of the day to service that particular effort and the country, that is, this country, to, in some way, lose its grip on that particular project, it is not only corruption to the hilt, but various other criminal elements must also be attached to it. Sir, Sri Lanka\u2019s past had been inundated by various governments at various times acting in such a way and in fact, the accusations of parties in Opposition at that time, including the present NPP Government\u2019s chief partner, the JVP, as and when those governments acted in that way, had been that the governments of the day had been bought over by various forces. Whenever the JVP sat in Opposition in the past, it had been probably the most vociferous of parties, accusing whichever government that was in power at various times with regard to not just of corruption, but also of being blatantly sold out to foreign powers\u2019 interests. That is a very serious allegation to make. Today, such a party, the JVP, is the primary partner of the NPP Government. The question is, what actions has this Government taken with regard to those several projects that the JVP, at that time, blatantly accused the government of the day of having sold out to foreign powers? Now, the first and foremost project that comes to mind is the Hambantota Harbour Project. The"
